# Testing conventions (ADR-0006)

## Pyramid

- **Unit** (`pnpm test` / `test:watch`): schemas, `*.domain.ts`, `authed`, pure helpers.
  Colocate as `src/**/*.test.ts`. No database.
- **Integration** (`pnpm test:integration`): call `*.handlers.ts` against Postgres
  database **`app_test`** (Compose locally; GHA service in CI). Never target `app`.
- **Storybook** (`pnpm test:storybook`): component interaction / a11y.
- **E2E** (`pnpm test:e2e`): thin user journeys; Playwright, no playwright-bdd.
- **Smoke** (`pnpm test:smoke`): read-only checks against deployed `APP_URL` (ADR-0007).

## Do

- Document features under `tests/integration/features/<name>/` and
  `tests/e2e/features/<name>/` with a short README + Given/When/Then comments.
- Extract growing rules into `*.domain.ts` so unit tests stay the majority.
- Reset `app_test` between integration tests (truncate / transaction helpers).
- Keep smoke tests read-only — never mutate shared hosted environments.

## Do not

- Use Testcontainers, Cucumber, or playwright-bdd in this template.
- Point integration `DATABASE_URL` at the long-lived `app` database.
- Invoke `createServerFn` results from tests — call handlers instead (ADR-0005).
- Mock Postgres in unit tests to fake SQL coverage.

See `docs/testing-strategy.md`, `docs/adr/0006-testing-strategy.md`, and `docs/ci-cd.md`.
